windows-native-rocblas: oneMath (XeStrata's fork, tag xestrata-10) builds its rocBLAS backend on Windows in a cross
build from Linux only; this builds it in a build on Windows itself as well, where the backend finds HIP and rocBLAS
through their CMake packages (the ROCm SDK of AMD's Python packages). Applied by CMakeLists.txt in such a build only,
until the fork carries it. Nothing changes elsewhere.
---
diff --git a/src/blas/backends/CMakeLists.txt b/src/blas/backends/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/blas/backends/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/blas/backends/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #===============================================================================
 # Copyright 2020-2021 Intel Corporation
 # Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the cuBLAS and rocBLAS backends in a cross build for Windows.
+# Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the rocBLAS backend in a build on Windows itself.
 #
 # Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
 # you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
@@ -47,7 +48,7 @@ if(ENABLE_CUBLAS_BACKEND AND (UNIX OR CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING))
   add_subdirectory(cublas)
 endif()
 
-if(ENABLE_ROCBLAS_BACKEND AND (UNIX OR CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING))
+if(ENABLE_ROCBLAS_BACKEND AND (UNIX OR CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING OR WIN32))
   add_subdirectory(rocblas)
 endif()
 
